  "oral_argument": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ecaa56a7caa977ec65bfe63a645f857a3c4ba162cc4132ec5516e2dd96668875",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ecaa56a7caa9-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Scalia asked, \u201cWhat\u2019s in between?\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ecaa56a7caa977ec65bfe63a645f857a3c4ba162cc4132ec5516e2dd96668875",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ecaa56a7caa9-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kennedy asked, \u201cYou\u2019re supposed to stop dead in your tracks and not pull off on the shoulder?\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ecaa56a7caa977ec65bfe63a645f857a3c4ba162cc4132ec5516e2dd96668875",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ecaa56a7caa9-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Breyer, justice Breyer noted, \u201cMy problem is there is arguably not here a gradation.\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ecaa56a7caa977ec65bfe63a645f857a3c4ba162cc4132ec5516e2dd96668875",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ecaa56a7caa9-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 23,
              "start": 23
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Alito said, \u201cI wouldn\u2019t say that they didn\u2019t have a rational basis for dividing it.\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ecaa56a7caa977ec65bfe63a645f857a3c4ba162cc4132ec5516e2dd96668875",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ecaa56a7caa9-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 40,
              "start": 40
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Alito asked, \u201cIf a person is convicted of vehicular flight that causes death, is that aggressive conduct?\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ecaa56a7caa977ec65bfe63a645f857a3c4ba162cc4132ec5516e2dd96668875",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ecaa56a7caa9-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 41,
              "start": 41
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Chief Justice Roberts asked, \u201cDoesn\u2019t whether it\u2019s aggressive or not depend upon how it happened?\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ecaa56a7caa977ec65bfe63a645f857a3c4ba162cc4132ec5516e2dd96668875",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ecaa56a7caa9-0002-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 42,
              "start": 42
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Scalia responded, \u201cBut he\u2019s saying even when it\u2019s risky, it\u2019s not aggressive.\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ecaa56a7caa977ec65bfe63a645f857a3c4ba162cc4132ec5516e2dd96668875",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ecaa56a7caa9-0002-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 44,
              "start": 44
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Breyer asked, \u201cSuppose you have one of 36 States which treat the general offense as a misdemeanor and then make it a felony if you put somebody at risk\u2026 would that be your normal instinct?\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ecaa56a7caa977ec65bfe63a645f857a3c4ba162cc4132ec5516e2dd96668875",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ecaa56a7caa9-0002-0008"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 47,
              "start": 47
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Sotomayor asked, \u201cYou can\u2019t commit (B) without committing (A) first\u2026 how can it not be a lesser included?\u201d"
      }
    ],
